2026-01-31 00:46:15 [simon@midnightblue] commodore64 archive?
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] Most C64 preservation archives are actually on the clearnet and safer to access there:
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Primary Resources*
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Archive.org — Massive C64 software, disk images, and magazine collections (legal gray
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] area but widely preserved)
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • CSDB (Commodore Scene Database) — The definitive scene release database
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Lemon64 — Forums and game database
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • GB64 (GameBase 64) — Comprehensive game collection frontend
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Tor/Preservation Mirrors*
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] Some preservation groups do maintain onion mirrors, typically for:
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Avoiding takedown requests on rare or disputed titles
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Hosting in jurisdictions with stricter copyright enforcement
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • MAG forums or specific demo scene archives
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] Search Ahmia.fi for "C64" or "Commodore" — you'll find some scene preservation boards and
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] demo archives that mirror to Tor for redundancy.
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] • Legal Note*
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] Homebrew, demos, and scene releases are generally safe. Commercial ROMs exist in a legal gray zone
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] depending on your jurisdiction and whether you own original media. The Internet Archive's C64
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] collection operates under library/preservation exemptions in many regions.
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] 
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] For actual gaming, VICE emulator + legally purchased C64 Mini/Maxi ROM packs, or
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] the C64 Forever commercial package keeps you clean.
2026-01-31 00:46:29 [kimi-k2.5] 
